\f1\b\fs48 \cf0 \strokec2 Phase 2 Outcome\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs24 \cf0 At the end of Phase 2, the project evolved from a 
\f1\b thread-safe single-node key-value store
\f2\b0  into a 
\f1\b distributed six-node sharded key-value store
\f2\b0 . The system now supports deterministic key placement using consistent hashing with virtual nodes, transparent request forwarding between servers, identical routing decisions across all nodes, graceful cluster startup and shutdown, and comprehensive testing of correctness, distribution, concurrency, and end-to-end routing. This architecture forms the foundation for Phase 3, where replication and quorum-based consistency will be added.\
